---
title: Coming next
nav_title: Roadmap
description: skyBlip Go is available today. skyBlip Bravo, in development, will receive ADS-B in the aircraft, and a Go paired with a Bravo will make a skyBlip Tango. The Panel for glass cockpits and the skyPost ground stations are in design.
---

<header class="page-hero">
  <h1>Today skyBlip Go. Next, ADS-B on board.</h1>
  <p class="page-hero-subtitle">
    skyBlip Go and Go+ are available. skyBlip Bravo, an ADS-B receiver, is in
    development. The Panel and the skyPost stations are in design, on the same
    code base.
  </p>
</header>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">In the aircraft</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    skyBlip Go receives ADS-L and FLARM. It does not receive ADS-B on
    1090&nbsp;MHz, which airliners, business jets, helicopters and many touring
    aircraft transmit. skyBlip Bravo will receive it in the aircraft, with no
    ground station.
  </p>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">In development</p>
      <h3 id="tango">skyBlip Tan<span class="highlight">go</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        A skyBlip Go paired with a skyBlip Bravo. Bravo will receive ADS-B and
        pass it to the Go. The Go will show it on its radar with the ADS-L and
        FLARM traffic, and warn you about all three.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your phone will connect to the Go and get all the traffic in one
        stream. The Go will keep broadcasting your position in ADS-L.
      </p>
      <p>
        A pilot who buys a Tango to see the airliners will also be seen in
        ADS-L.
      </p>
      <p>
        A plain Go has no buzzer, so in a Tango the alarm will sound on Bravo.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        Bravo&rsquo;s hardware has not yet been tested with skyBlip. Reception,
        range and altitude handling remain unverified.
      </p>
      <p class="feature-guide"><small>Hardware: LilyGO T-Echo and Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1.</small></p>
    </div>
    <%= render "shared/tango" %>
  </div>

  <div class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3 id="bravo">skyBlip Bravo.</h3>
      <p>
        Card-sized, with no screen. It will receive ADS-B on 1090&nbsp;MHz,
        Extended Squitter (DF17) only. On its own, it will send that traffic to
        your navigation app and sound the alarm. It will not broadcast your
        position: to be seen, pair it with a Go.
      </p>
      <p class="note">Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>skyBlip Tango+.</h3>
      <p>
        A Go+ paired with a Bravo, with the same traffic as a Tango. The Go+
        has its own buzzer and vibration motor, and will take over the alarm
        while the pair is healthy.
      </p>
      <p class="note">LilyGO T-Echo Plus and Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">For glass cockpits</p>
      <h3>skyBlip <span class="highlight">Panel</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        A fixed box behind the instrument panel, powered by the aircraft. No
        screen: the traffic shows on the panel display, Garmin G3X, Dynon
        SkyView and the others, like a factory traffic source.
      </p>
      <p>
        ADS-L transmit and receive. RS-232 outputs (FLARM NMEA or GDL90) to the
        EFIS, GDL90 over Wi-Fi, FLARM NMEA over Bluetooth.
      </p>
      <p class="feature-guide"><small>Hardware: LilyGO T-Beam Supreme, MAX3232 RS-232 adapter.</small></p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot shot--photo">
      <%= pages_image_tag "skyblip-panel-board.avif", alt: "skyBlip Panel: the board in its case, with its antenna" %>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">On the ground</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Around the airfield, a skyPost station will receive ADS-B, add the traffic
    of the Open Glider Network and the weather (QNH, METAR, TAF), and relay it
    all in ADS-L to every skyBlip Go in range.
  </p>
  <div class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3>skyPost Helio.</h3>
      <p>The solar station. Self-powered, in a weatherproof case on a mast. Will receive ADS-B, ADS-L and FLARM.</p>
      <p class="note">LilyGO T-Beam Supreme, Ebyte E80-900MBL 1090 receiver, LilyGO T-Solar kit.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>skyPost Bridge.</h3>
      <p>For existing stations: OGN, PiAware, adsb.lol. Will relay in ADS-L the traffic they already decode, without touching their feeds.</p>
      <p class="note">LilyGO T-Beam Supreme.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%= render "shared/cta" %>
</section>
